cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "synthscore: target-class calibrated synthesizability scoring"
abstract: >-
  Synthesizability scores are deployed as hard filters with a single global
  cutoff. Measured against 26,947 ChEMBL compounds that each carry a recorded
  activity, and are therefore known to have been synthesized, those cutoffs
  discard real chemistry at rates that depend on the target class rather than
  the molecule: SAscore at its published cutoff of 6.0 rejects 9.48% of
  whole-cell antibacterial compounds and 0.29% of nuclear-receptor compounds.
  This package supplies per-target-class operating points calibrated to a
  declared false-reject rate, and a tool that applies them.
authors:
  - family-names: "Tiwari"
    given-names: "Harshita"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - synthetic accessibility
  - synthesizability
  - cheminformatics
  - de novo design
  - calibration
  - ChEMBL
